# %% NORA task decomposition v6.1 - one sequential pipeline
#
#   PHASE 1   Read the data                  only the columns the decomposition needs (intent is never loaded)
#   PHASE 2   Prepare the calls              time order, each call counted once, system, agent, outcome
#   PHASE 3   Event log                      every interaction as ordered steps (agent . API)
#   PHASE 4   Hand-off detection             calls with which the coordinator passes work to another agent
#   PHASE 5   The model                      (a) which hand-offs bring work   (b) classes   (c) task DAG per class
#   PHASE 6   Validation                     k-fold cross-validation: learn on k-1 folds, test on the unseen fold
#   PHASE 7   Final model                    the model refitted on all interactions
#   PHASE 8   Approved traces                follow their plan and are not anomalous (isolation forest)
#   PHASE 9   API errors                     where each failure sits (HTTP status class, RFC 9110)
#   PHASE 10  Outputs                        decomposition workbook, validation workbook, report.md, metrics.json
#
# Every name, system, agent and threshold comes from the data or from a named standard; nothing is typed in by hand.

